### Intent Override Mechanism

The webhook (`index.js`) implements a runtime override system as a safety net: when a user is inside an active multi-turn flow (appointment or quote) and types cancel/goodbye/escalation keywords that Dialogflow misroutes to the current flow-step intent, the handler is replaced with `handleCancelarProceso`, `handleGoodbye`, or `handleDerivarAgente`. The 10 FAQ/utility intents are marked as `NON_OVERRIDABLE`. Note: `cancelar_proceso`, `derivar_agente_humano`, and `despedida` also exist as real Dialogflow intents, so the override only fires when Dialogflow fails to match them directly.

